theo-pod (t-169): reject sampling-frequency indices above 11

The ADTS header, the program config element and the AudioSpecificConfig
SBR extension carry a 4-bit sampling-frequency index, but samp_rate_info[]
has 12 entries (12 to 14 are reserved, 15 is an explicit frequency this
decoder does not support). Only the AudioSpecificConfig base index was
checked; the others reached infoinit(), the SBR set-up and
PVMP4AudioDecoderDisableAacPlus() and read past the table. Each source now
rejects indices above 11, infoinit() refuses them, and
PVMP4AudioDecoderDisableAacPlus() only restores and reads a valid index.
Found by the host fuzzer (UBSan index out of bounds in infoinit and
PVMP4AudioDecoderDisableAacPlus, ASan global-buffer-overflow in infoinit);
regression inputs tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-sampling-index-adts.bin
and t169-sampling-index-pce.bin.

